{"gold":[{"independent_answer":"4","question_sha256":"aa5c2aab758e2fe2c205b7491ae51e29c869f2a2deb0b0f9bb33b3a4a29855c3","reason":"The closing speed is 24-15=9 mph. Covering the 0.6-mile lead takes 0.6/9=1/15 hour, and (1/15)*60=4 minutes, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-4873"},{"independent_answer":"2","question_sha256":"8fa312d77976a3f01dab0432f5acecb18cdf8015120cabd3adf71191f6f6621b","reason":"He uses 12-2=10 gallons. He drives 5+5=10 miles for the supermarket trip and 2+2+6=10 miles for the interrupted farm trip, totaling 20 miles. Thus 20/10=2 miles per gallon, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-338"},{"independent_answer":"105","question_sha256":"77df2250558ae7f9fef3504b464158a756828a2a8a1a01caeb2b823897ad5b52","reason":"Four hours is 240 minutes, so she writes 240*10=2400 words and earns $240 from words. Three articles add 3*$60=$180, giving $420 total; $420/4=$105 per hour, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-4631"},{"independent_answer":"3","question_sha256":"c8b93ea7e6b2138d8f2a1a117ab86a2dbe4ee6851ac6a8144492221947bc14b3","reason":"Janet crosses in 60/30=2 hours, while her sister crosses in 60/12=5 hours. Janet waits 5-2=3 hours, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-4488"},{"independent_answer":"2","question_sha256":"60e0b0279d590fa1e47a5f7726453f5bcd8c8dec3e8cc36ce920802f6d13d722","reason":"Against the current, Karen's effective speed is 10-4=6 mph. The time is 12/6=2 hours, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5662"},{"independent_answer":"28000","question_sha256":"ab0511079b09c752114142c4772076b27ef39680442bcc37fdb4a9a2f506c7a7","reason":"Each rep earns 8*$14=$112 per day. For 50 reps over 5 days, the total is $112*50*5=$28,000, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-3086"},{"independent_answer":"10","question_sha256":"040c266d5b6a111710d8bca48a6f3ca78f2dd8e2f626e5e8f19df52c67afbf03","reason":"The capacity lasts 240000/1000=240 hours of continuous rain. Converting gives 240/24=10 days, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1751"},{"independent_answer":"18","question_sha256":"30314f07e441c26b8a575cf82cebfa82f146d852b7d889a24c626f44eb7f321b","reason":"The 90-mile trip requires 90/3=30 gallons total. Since 12 gallons are already in the tank, the driver must add 30-12=18 gallons, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-3624"}],"reviews":[{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["Relative speed = 24 mph - 15 mph = 9 mph","Time (in minutes) = 0.0667 hours * 60 minutes/hour = 4 minutes"],"first_person":false,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":true,"key":"gsm8k-train-4873:rich","neutral_prefix_compatible":true,"no_padding":true,"prefix_reason":"The computations are supportable from the question and ordinary arithmetic, with no claim of hidden feedback or an external checking event.","raw_call_sha256":"0f2cd2837400634db7c429d811f88744bcc23f29c4b9b786e98b2dd964809a0c","reason":"The response correctly subtracts the speeds, divides the lead by the 9-mph closing speed, and converts the resulting time to 4 minutes. Its numerical intermediates are checkable and its relative-speed method is reusable, but the entire account is impersonal and contains no substantive first-person account of performing or checking the operations.","reusable_content":true,"status":"FAIL","student_prefix_sha256":"07253f6ee42362e1b91b5cc8c7bbe3b0887fe233520b98b12b6219292d2f55b9","target_sha256":"8173e1a9a00518ec45d7bab33fa889c44e8137be1d8c474cdf3b7a54677b639b"},{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["I first calculated the relative speed of the dog compared to the rabbit","Difference in distance covered = 1.6 miles - 1 mile = 0.6 miles, which matches the rabbit's head start"],"first_person":true,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":true,"key":"gsm8k-train-4873:new_record","neutral_prefix_compatible":true,"no_padding":true,"prefix_reason":"